DECLTAG|CompareDoubleWithZero U:G:32, U:F:64, ZD:G:32|arm64|arm64 ppc64|+ppc64
COMMENT|CompareDoubleWithZero U:G:32, U:F:64, ZD:G:32|# The WithZero family is claimed. It took three attempts, and the middle one is\n# worth leaving here because the symptom pointed away from the cause.\n#\n# Tagging it made three testb3 groups abort inside Inst::generate --\n# testConstDoubleCompareZero, testDoubleLiteralComparison and\n# testConvertDoubleToFloatEqual -- with the Inst being exactly the form\n# declared below (op=296 n=3 kinds DoubleCond, Tmp, Tmp, read out of the Inst's\n# own storage because args() is inlined and `this` is optimised out at the\n# crash). The crash was the TERMINAL RELEASE_ASSERT_NOT_REACHED of\n# Inst::generate, which every non-matching path tail-calls to, so the frame\n# said nothing and the dispatch appeared to contradict itself.\n#\n# It did not. Rebuilding AirGenerated.cpp with #pragma clang optimize off named\n# it in one frame: MacroAssembler::compareDoubleWithZero, the SHARED one.\n# MacroAssembler.h defined it under #if !CPU(X86_64) && !CPU(ARM64) as an\n# UNREACHABLE_FOR_PLATFORM, and since MacroAssembler derives from\n# MacroAssemblerPPC64 that definition HIDES the port's rather than overriding\n# it. The same guard was also hiding the port's compareDouble behind a branchy\n# fallback, silently and without failing anything. Same shape as the\n# pushToSaveByteOffset hiding in jsc-ppc64le-b3-air.md section 8.3; the guard\n# now excludes PPC64LE and an audit of every such guard in MacroAssembler.h\n# found exactly these two live on this target.
DECLTAG|CompareFloatWithZero U:G:32, U:F:32, ZD:G:32|arm64|arm64 ppc64|+ppc64
DECLTAG|Branch64 U:G:32, U:G:64, U:G:64 /branch|64|64 ppc64|+ppc64
DECLTAG|BranchTest64 U:G:32, U:G:64, U:G:64 /branch|64|64 ppc64|+ppc64
DECLTAG|BranchDoubleWithZero U:G:32, U:F:64 /branch|arm64|arm64 ppc64|+ppc64
DECLTAG|BranchFloatWithZero U:G:32, U:F:32 /branch|arm64|arm64 ppc64|+ppc64
DECLTAG|BranchAdd64 U:G:32, U:G:64, U:G:64, ZD:G:64 /branch|64|64 ppc64|+ppc64
DECLTAG|BranchAdd64 U:G:32, U:G:64, UD:G:64 /branch|64|64 ppc64|+ppc64
FORMCOMMENT|BranchAdd64 U:G:32, U:G:64, UD:G:64 /branch|ResCond, Imm, Tmp|0|    # This form was held away from ppc64 by declaration while\n    # emitAdd64Overflow clobbered the operand it was handed. That fix is on\n    # the trunk now -- the helper computes r ^ b before r ^ a, and asserts the\n    # aliasing it tolerates -- so the tag comes off and the form is claimed.\n    # Re-measured rather than assumed, because this is the one form in the 64:\n    # set ever shown to produce wrong code that assembles cleanly: with a\n    # positive immediate the broken predicate missed all 8,390,656 real\n    # overflows, and twenty million uniformly random operand pairs produced no\n    # disagreement at all. See powerpc64le-handbook\n    # docs/jsc-ppc64le-air-opcode-tags.md section 4.1.
FORMTAG|BranchMul32 U:G:32, U:G:32, U:G:32, ZD:G:32 /branch|ResCond, Tmp, Tmp, Tmp|0|arm64|arm64 ppc64|+ppc64
DECLTAG|BranchMul64 U:G:32, U:G:64, U:G:64, S:G:64, ZD:G:64 /branch|arm64|arm64 ppc64|+ppc64
